import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout lang="en" title="Contact" description="How to reach HSL Lab's blog, projects and portfolio with error reports, correction requests, feedback or collaboration questions, and what to include.">
  <header class="page-top"><div class="article-shell"><div class="section-kicker">Contact</div><h1>Contact</h1><p>Error reports, correction requests, feedback and collaboration questions go to email or to the comments on each page.</p></div></header>
  <div class="article-body article-shell">
    <h2>Email</h2>
    <p><a href="mailto:coolwin200@gmail.com">coolwin200@gmail.com</a></p>
    <h2>Where to send what</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Errors or opinions about a <a href="/en/blog/">blog</a> article: the comments under it, or email</li>
      <li>Backseat advice on the <a href="/en/projects/">projects</a> (beating the KMA, the AI investing duel): the comments on the project page</li>
      <li>Questions about methods or code in the <a href="/en/stories/">project stories</a>: email</li>
      <li>Collaboration or research questions after reading the <a href="/en/portfolio/">portfolio</a>: email</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Errors and corrections</h2>
    <p>If something is wrong, send the article URL and the source that shows it. Confirmed errors are fixed and the updated date advances. A comment under the article works too.</p>
    <p>For prices or specs that differ by market, say which country and when you checked; it makes the fix faster.</p>
    <h2>Partnerships and advertising</h2>
    <p>Partnerships or sponsorships do not change editorial judgments, and any commercial relationship is labeled clearly in the article concerned. The editorial principles are on the <a href="/en/blog/about/">about and editorial policy</a> page.</p>
    <h2>Privacy</h2>
    <p>How what you send is handled is described in the <a href="/en/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.</p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
